Opt-in native LRAT for the wallcc leaf engine (direction 4 of smx0er1f6).

Apply with:  patch -p1 --batch --forward -i 0001-lrat-optin.patch
             (from the repository root; touches only tools/color-resolved-wallcc/)

Default behaviour is unchanged: without --lrat-trim nothing in the new module
runs, leaves stay binary DRAT, and the joined cas.drat+leaf DRAT replay is the
same code path as before.  With --lrat-trim PATH (and --engine native) the leaf
engine emits native binary LRAT, the leaf is checked by that exact checker
against the exact bytes the solver read, and one extra per-run premise is
established first: every clause appended to the parent is a RUP consequence of
the parent.  Fail-closed: a missing/unexecutable/mismatched checker, a failed
premise, a checker exit other than 20, or an artifact that does not parse as a
complete refutation make the leaf CHECK_FAILED or abort the run; OPEN is never
evidence.
